{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Like the ledge of the altar.</b> Rashi's interpretation: thus we learned in Zevachim — what is the ledge? Between horn and horn, and inward from them one cubit, for the going of the priests' feet. These two cubits are called כרכב. At each of the corners of the altar, which was square, there extended one cubit by one cubit, one cubit high, and these are what are called the horns of the altar. And that one cubit that was on top of the altar between horn and horn, along each of its four sides; and another cubit inward from it — these two cubits are called כרכוב, as Rashi interpreted."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:00:40.463745888Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}